// Advanced Settings folders at the bottom: "Team Settings" (Teamplay, Disable [colour] Team; hidden in Capture the Bag / Assault) and "Spawn Settings" (Team Spawns, Respawn Delay / team delays). Advanced Settings keeps Disable Unarmed, Mercy Rule, Number of Flames, Zone Scoring Interval. Settings that can never apply to a mode are left out: modes that can never have teams (Deathmatch, Elimination, Vampire, Flame Tag, Virus, Monkey Assistant...) show no Team Settings folder and no Team Spawns item, and the Spawn Settings folder is left out too when it would be empty (Gladiator counts as a team mode because Team VIP can turn teams on). Layout: same look as the match settings page (small upper-case items); the mode's own settings come first, then Disable Unarmed, Mercy Rule, Multikill Bonus Window, Infinite Ammo, then the folder links ("Team Settings >", "Spawn Settings >")
